<title>AUSTRALIA: RUGBY UNION-FRANCE BEAT VICTORIA 65-13 IN TOUR MATCH.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-FRANCE BEAT VICTORIA 65-13 IN TOUR MATCH.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>France beat Victoria 65-13 (halftime 34-8) in a rugby union tour match at Olympic Park on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>France - Tries: Richard Dourthe (3), Sebastien Viars (2), Thomas Castaignede), Pierre Bondouy, David Aucagne, Olivier Magne, Pierre Raschi, Christophe Lamaison. Conversions: Richard Dourthe (5).</p>
<p>Victoria - Tries: Matthew Nasalio (2). Penalty: Andrew Hendry.</p>
</text>
